WEBVTT

00:00:00.043 --> 00:00:01.044
GridBot Builder.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.784
GridBot Blueprint.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:04.090
Lesson one.

00:00:04.626 --> 00:00:05.376
Introduction.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:07.616
Education only.

00:00:08.175 --> 00:00:09.489
Not financial advice.

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:12.061
This is general information and

00:00:12.061 --> 00:00:14.264
doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:16.164
financial situation or needs.

00:00:16.684 --> 00:00:18.448
Crypto is high risk; you could

00:00:18.448 --> 00:00:20.139
lose all the money you put in.

00:00:20.659 --> 00:00:22.724
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:22.724 --> 00:00:24.434
indicator of future results.

00:00:25.484 --> 00:00:27.540
The prices are public historical

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.302
daily closes, marked Example.

00:00:29.822 --> 00:00:31.889
A close is the last price of the day.

00:00:33.044 --> 00:00:34.943
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:00:35.942 --> 00:00:37.841
By the end of this series you will

00:00:37.841 --> 00:00:40.076
understand what a grid bot does, when it

00:00:40.076 --> 00:00:42.310
can capture bounces, and where it loses.

00:00:42.772 --> 00:00:44.783
You will know how to plan one, test

00:00:44.783 --> 00:00:46.682
it on paper, run it, check it, and

00:00:46.682 --> 00:00:48.730
change the capital you give to bots

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.591
only under written risk rules.

00:00:51.111 --> 00:00:52.508
This is education, not

00:00:52.508 --> 00:00:53.828
a promise of results.

00:00:54.878 --> 00:00:56.488
Price often moves sideways,

00:00:56.488 --> 00:00:58.239
bouncing between the same top

00:00:58.239 --> 00:00:59.989
and bottom instead of leaving.

00:01:00.509 --> 00:01:02.087
A grid is a ladder of limit

00:01:02.087 --> 00:01:04.040
orders built for that bouncing.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.416
When price runs one way and stays

00:01:06.416 --> 00:01:08.539
there, the bot has nothing left to do.

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:12.120
Crypto is digital money, such as bitcoin.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.316
You do not need to have bought

00:01:14.316 --> 00:01:15.601
any before this lesson.

00:01:15.979 --> 00:01:17.947
An exchange is the website or app

00:01:17.947 --> 00:01:20.279
where you swap Australian dollars for

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:22.319
crypto, and crypto back to dollars.

00:01:22.839 --> 00:01:24.515
This course does not name one,

00:01:24.515 --> 00:01:26.191
and it does not send an order.

00:01:26.936 --> 00:01:28.500
Cash is money you can spend.

00:01:28.902 --> 00:01:30.802
Here that means dollars, or a coin

00:01:30.802 --> 00:01:32.925
that is meant to stay near one dollar.

00:01:33.232 --> 00:01:35.423
Coin is the crypto, such as bitcoin.

00:01:36.473 --> 00:01:38.820
An order is an instruction to buy or sell.

00:01:39.272 --> 00:01:41.079
A buy order swaps cash for coin.

00:01:41.599 --> 00:01:43.963
A sell order swaps coin back to cash, and

00:01:43.963 --> 00:01:46.327
you can only sell coin you already hold.

00:01:47.377 --> 00:01:49.742
A grid bot places waiting buy orders

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.870
on lines below the price and sell

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:53.998
orders on lines above it, inside a

00:01:53.998 --> 00:01:55.732
top and a bottom you choose.

00:01:56.252 --> 00:01:57.928
The space between your top and

00:01:57.928 --> 00:01:59.660
your bottom is called the band.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:01.875
The sells need some coin, so a grid

00:02:01.875 --> 00:02:03.824
starts with part cash and part

00:02:03.824 --> 00:02:05.774
coin, and that is a description,

00:02:05.774 --> 00:02:07.645
not advice about what to hold.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:10.401
A limit order is an order that

00:02:10.401 --> 00:02:11.966
waits at a price you choose.

00:02:12.485 --> 00:02:14.049
It does not chase the price.

00:02:14.469 --> 00:02:16.033
Chasing the price would mean

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:17.485
moving the order to follow

00:02:17.485 --> 00:02:19.050
wherever the price has gone.

00:02:19.899 --> 00:02:21.974
An order fills when the price reaches

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:23.706
its line and the trade happens.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:26.374
Until then, the order is only waiting.

00:02:27.424 --> 00:02:29.379
Think of a ladder leaned on a wall.

00:02:29.521 --> 00:02:31.867
The rungs wait, and they do not chase you.

00:02:32.143 --> 00:02:34.433
A rung is one price where an order waits.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:37.019
The gap is the space between two rungs.

00:02:37.838 --> 00:02:39.738
Setting the band uses three words.

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:41.544
The range is the top rung

00:02:41.544 --> 00:02:42.672
and the bottom rung.

00:02:43.192 --> 00:02:45.315
The levels are the rungs between them.

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:47.956
The stop is the written rule for leaving.

00:02:48.805 --> 00:02:50.845
A grid has three parts you can name:

00:02:50.845 --> 00:02:52.856
the range, the levels, and the stop.

00:02:53.333 --> 00:02:54.562
The range is the band.

00:02:55.072 --> 00:02:57.028
The levels are the rungs inside it.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.921
The range is the top line and the

00:02:59.921 --> 00:03:01.764
bottom line, taken from the path.

00:03:02.243 --> 00:03:03.695
Every close in this window

00:03:03.695 --> 00:03:05.427
stayed between those two lines.

00:03:06.213 --> 00:03:08.053
The range is a top and a bottom

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:09.586
you draw before any rung.

00:03:10.106 --> 00:03:11.614
Without a top and a bottom,

00:03:11.614 --> 00:03:13.067
you can't place the lines.

00:03:14.129 --> 00:03:16.721
Six equal gaps of about 900 dollars sit

00:03:16.721 --> 00:03:19.393
between the bottom line and the top line.

00:03:19.913 --> 00:03:22.140
Each gap is about 900 dollars:

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:24.367
the top line minus the bottom

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:25.852
line, divided by six.

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:27.707
It is one step between

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.190
lines, not the whole band.

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.549
Seven lines make those six gaps.

00:03:32.069 --> 00:03:33.857
The levels are the prices on the

00:03:33.857 --> 00:03:35.533
rungs where limit orders wait.

00:03:36.519 --> 00:03:38.028
The levels are limit orders

00:03:38.028 --> 00:03:39.313
that wait on the rungs.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:41.306
A limit order sits at a price.

00:03:41.809 --> 00:03:42.842
It does not chase.

00:03:44.042 --> 00:03:46.333
Buy orders wait on lines below the price.

00:03:46.768 --> 00:03:48.724
Sell orders wait on lines above it.

00:03:49.205 --> 00:03:50.322
You choose the band,

00:03:50.322 --> 00:03:51.607
the gaps and the money.

00:03:51.891 --> 00:03:53.344
The bot places each order.

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:56.765
Buy orders sit on lines below the price

00:03:56.765 --> 00:03:59.028
and sell orders sit on lines above it.

00:03:59.548 --> 00:04:01.623
An order fills when the price reaches

00:04:01.623 --> 00:04:03.355
its line and the trade happens.

00:04:03.817 --> 00:04:05.956
The sells need some coin, so a grid

00:04:05.956 --> 00:04:08.253
starts with part cash and part coin,

00:04:08.253 --> 00:04:10.629
and that is a description, not advice.

00:04:11.829 --> 00:04:13.622
After a fill, the bot places the

00:04:13.622 --> 00:04:15.343
opposite order one rung away.

00:04:15.863 --> 00:04:18.042
A buy fill gets a sell one rung higher.

00:04:18.428 --> 00:04:20.658
A sell fill gets a buy one rung lower.

00:04:21.178 --> 00:04:22.798
You still write the stop, and

00:04:22.798 --> 00:04:24.474
you act when that rule is met.

00:04:24.705 --> 00:04:26.940
The bot does not decide the stop for you

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:29.063
unless you turned that setting on, and

00:04:29.063 --> 00:04:31.130
you write which one before you start.

00:04:31.864 --> 00:04:33.205
Think of a market stall.

00:04:33.637 --> 00:04:35.751
The stallholder buys stock a little

00:04:35.751 --> 00:04:37.865
cheaper and sells it a little dearer,

00:04:37.865 --> 00:04:39.485
and pays a fee on every sale.

00:04:39.936 --> 00:04:41.663
A grid can do that while price

00:04:41.663 --> 00:04:43.103
bounces inside the band.

00:04:43.623 --> 00:04:46.144
A bounce means price moves down and back

00:04:46.144 --> 00:04:48.513
up, or up and back down, and stays inside.

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:51.269
One buy at a lower line and the later

00:04:51.269 --> 00:04:53.352
sell of that same coin is one pair.

00:04:53.872 --> 00:04:56.111
On these daily closes the summer window

00:04:56.111 --> 00:04:58.147
finished only three one-step pairs.

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:00.399
The sell line is higher, so the

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.242
cash that comes back is more than

00:05:02.242 --> 00:05:04.197
the cash that left, before the fee.

00:05:04.491 --> 00:05:05.943
A fee is what the exchange

00:05:05.943 --> 00:05:07.507
charges when an order fills.

00:05:07.688 --> 00:05:09.309
The fee comes out of the gap.

00:05:09.536 --> 00:05:11.267
If the fees are larger than the

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:12.832
gap, the pair keeps nothing.

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:14.256
This is not a promise.

00:05:14.776 --> 00:05:16.579
The pair finishes only if price

00:05:16.579 --> 00:05:18.453
does bounce and both orders fill.

00:05:19.503 --> 00:05:20.732
The daily close is the

00:05:20.732 --> 00:05:21.961
last price of the day.

00:05:22.381 --> 00:05:24.181
Crypto trades all day, so the

00:05:24.181 --> 00:05:25.590
day is cut at a set time.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:28.715
The daily close is at 11am Australian

00:05:28.715 --> 00:05:31.405
eastern daylight time while daylight

00:05:31.405 --> 00:05:34.263
saving is in force, and at 10am Australian

00:05:34.263 --> 00:05:36.617
eastern standard time otherwise.

00:05:37.137 --> 00:05:39.121
This is a simple candle that shows

00:05:39.121 --> 00:05:40.797
the day's high, low and close.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.200
Traders call it a candle because

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.129
the full version has a thick body

00:05:45.129 --> 00:05:46.861
and a thin wick, like a candle.

00:05:47.293 --> 00:05:48.801
Here we only need the high,

00:05:48.801 --> 00:05:50.030
the low and the close.

00:05:50.364 --> 00:05:53.543
This candle is 19 July 2023.

00:05:54.063 --> 00:05:55.292
The high, the low, and

00:05:55.292 --> 00:05:56.577
the close are labelled.

00:05:57.470 --> 00:05:59.599
The example is Bitcoin's public

00:05:59.599 --> 00:06:01.255
daily price in US dollars.

00:06:01.775 --> 00:06:04.974
From 19 July 2023 to 16 October

00:06:04.974 --> 00:06:07.917
2023, every one of those days

00:06:07.917 --> 00:06:10.348
closed inside the band.

00:06:10.868 --> 00:06:12.541
The close crossed the seven

00:06:12.541 --> 00:06:14.287
lines 28 times in that window.

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:17.119
The count is an example, not a forecast.

00:06:17.639 --> 00:06:19.427
We do not need to read each day.

00:06:19.693 --> 00:06:21.035
The shape is the lesson,

00:06:21.035 --> 00:06:22.449
and it is marked Example.

00:06:23.499 --> 00:06:26.433
Those 28 crossings are not 28 results.

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:29.155
A crossing only means the close moved

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:31.222
from one side of a line to the other.

00:06:31.664 --> 00:06:33.375
A pair is finished only when a

00:06:33.375 --> 00:06:35.229
buy and its later sell have both

00:06:35.229 --> 00:06:36.961
filled, and only after the fee.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:39.360
The price can cross many lines and

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:41.259
still leave you holding coin if it

00:06:41.259 --> 00:06:42.879
walks out through the bottom.

00:06:43.416 --> 00:06:46.397
In this example a buy waiting at the

00:06:46.397 --> 00:06:49.686
lower of these two lines was reached on

00:06:49.686 --> 00:06:52.667
17 August 2023, and the sell one line

00:06:52.667 --> 00:06:55.648
above was reached on 29 August 2023.

00:06:56.168 --> 00:06:57.956
The card shows the gap, then the

00:06:57.956 --> 00:06:59.520
two fees, then what is left.

00:06:59.829 --> 00:07:01.617
Say it as about eight and a half

00:07:01.617 --> 00:07:03.796
dollars after fees, for one small pair.

00:07:04.245 --> 00:07:06.145
It happens only if the price comes

00:07:06.145 --> 00:07:07.821
back up through the sell line.

00:07:07.925 --> 00:07:09.656
If the price leaves through the

00:07:09.656 --> 00:07:11.444
bottom, you still hold the coin,

00:07:11.444 --> 00:07:13.008
and the pair never finishes.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.988
This card is not money you made.

00:07:15.916 --> 00:07:17.704
Now watch what you hold when the

00:07:17.704 --> 00:07:19.715
price leaves the band and stays out.

00:07:19.978 --> 00:07:21.599
Above the band the sells have

00:07:21.599 --> 00:07:23.386
filled and you are holding cash,

00:07:23.386 --> 00:07:24.839
with nothing left to sell.

00:07:25.243 --> 00:07:26.807
Below the band the buys have

00:07:26.807 --> 00:07:28.260
filled and you are holding

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:29.992
coin, with nothing left to buy.

00:07:31.804 --> 00:07:33.648
A fill is that trade at the line.

00:07:34.035 --> 00:07:36.435
As price climbs, each sell order fills.

00:07:36.635 --> 00:07:38.167
So you end up holding cash.

00:07:38.687 --> 00:07:41.090
As price falls, each buy order fills.

00:07:41.291 --> 00:07:42.799
So you end up holding coin.

00:07:44.942 --> 00:07:47.177
Here is that stop rule on the real path.

00:07:47.598 --> 00:07:49.959
It triggers if a daily close is outside

00:07:49.959 --> 00:07:52.246
the band, through the top or the bottom,

00:07:52.246 --> 00:07:54.754
and the next daily close is still outside.

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:56.727
Then the idea is finished.

00:07:57.107 --> 00:07:59.201
You stop the bot, which cancels the

00:07:59.201 --> 00:08:01.070
waiting orders, and do what you

00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:03.164
wrote: keep the coin or swap to cash.

00:08:03.684 --> 00:08:05.665
A bot's automatic stop is a price

00:08:05.665 --> 00:08:07.353
that can fire during the day.

00:08:07.873 --> 00:08:10.088
This course uses the two daily closes,

00:08:10.088 --> 00:08:12.159
unless you wrote that price stop on.

00:08:12.679 --> 00:08:14.813
On 23 October 2023 the close

00:08:14.813 --> 00:08:17.225
finished above the top line, and

00:08:17.225 --> 00:08:19.544
the next day was still above it.

00:08:20.594 --> 00:08:22.214
The stop is your written rule

00:08:22.214 --> 00:08:23.667
for when you stop the bot.

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:26.032
Through the top, the sells

00:08:26.032 --> 00:08:27.708
have filled and you hold cash.

00:08:27.817 --> 00:08:29.661
Through the bottom, the buys have

00:08:29.661 --> 00:08:31.504
filled and you hold coin that you

00:08:31.504 --> 00:08:33.515
bought above where the price is now.

00:08:33.874 --> 00:08:35.327
That loss can keep growing

00:08:35.327 --> 00:08:36.444
until the stop acts.

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:38.593
You stop the bot either way, then

00:08:38.593 --> 00:08:40.157
you follow the written rule.

00:08:40.266 --> 00:08:42.054
The bot does not decide the stop

00:08:42.054 --> 00:08:43.953
unless you turned that setting on.

00:08:44.756 --> 00:08:46.331
A common mistake is thinking

00:08:46.331 --> 00:08:47.839
the bot predicts the price.

00:08:48.628 --> 00:08:49.378
It does not.

00:08:49.944 --> 00:08:50.726
It only waits.

00:08:51.096 --> 00:08:52.604
Another mistake is starting

00:08:52.604 --> 00:08:53.777
with no written stop.

00:08:54.722 --> 00:08:55.951
There is no promise of

00:08:55.951 --> 00:08:57.236
results in this lesson.

00:08:57.427 --> 00:08:59.035
Numbers marked Example are

00:08:59.035 --> 00:09:00.713
teaching numbers, not advice.

00:09:01.913 --> 00:09:04.305
Paper or demo trading is like driving

00:09:04.305 --> 00:09:06.389
with L-plates: you practise with

00:09:06.389 --> 00:09:08.859
pretend money before anything is real.

00:09:09.379 --> 00:09:10.896
Lesson 7 shows you how.

00:09:11.946 --> 00:09:13.633
This introduction is step one.

00:09:14.333 --> 00:09:15.395
Then what you need.

00:09:16.025 --> 00:09:17.552
Then exactly what a grid

00:09:17.552 --> 00:09:19.003
bot does, order by order.

00:09:20.003 --> 00:09:21.120
Then market regimes.

00:09:22.046 --> 00:09:23.734
This introduction is step one.

00:09:24.434 --> 00:09:25.496
Then what you need.

00:09:26.126 --> 00:09:27.653
Then exactly what a grid

00:09:27.653 --> 00:09:29.104
bot does, order by order.

00:09:29.804 --> 00:09:31.699
Then market regimes, spacing

00:09:31.699 --> 00:09:33.516
and range, and entry and exit.

00:09:34.216 --> 00:09:35.612
Then a paper test, weekly

00:09:35.612 --> 00:09:37.176
checks, and common mistakes.

00:09:37.856 --> 00:09:39.868
Then scaling up under written rules,

00:09:39.868 --> 00:09:41.823
and an opt-in lesson on liquidation

00:09:41.823 --> 00:09:43.164
with your complete plan.

00:09:44.172 --> 00:09:45.257
Then a paper test.

00:09:45.977 --> 00:09:47.039
Then weekly checks.

00:09:47.776 --> 00:09:48.964
Then common mistakes.

00:09:49.664 --> 00:09:51.675
Then scaling up under written rules.

00:09:52.486 --> 00:09:54.385
The next lesson is a checklist you

00:09:54.385 --> 00:09:56.285
write on paper, before any screen.

00:09:57.306 --> 00:09:59.472
The next step is the setup checklist,

00:09:59.472 --> 00:10:01.060
on paper, before any screen.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:03.480
You will need the three words when

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.435
that checklist asks what a grid is.

00:10:06.472 --> 00:10:07.478
Keep one sentence.

00:10:07.768 --> 00:10:09.947
A grid waits, it buys lower and sells

00:10:09.947 --> 00:10:12.202
higher while price bounces, the fees

00:10:12.202 --> 00:10:14.157
come out of the gap, and if a daily

00:10:14.157 --> 00:10:16.336
close leaves and stays out, you stop

00:10:16.336 --> 00:10:18.590
the bot and follow the rule you wrote.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:21.219
If you keep one sentence,

00:10:21.219 --> 00:10:22.956
keep this: range, levels, and

00:10:22.956 --> 00:10:24.772
stop, drawn before any click.

00:10:25.292 --> 00:10:26.935
Bouncing inside the band is

00:10:26.935 --> 00:10:28.331
what a grid is built for.

00:10:28.812 --> 00:10:30.049
The exit from the band

00:10:30.049 --> 00:10:31.355
is the failure picture.

00:10:32.589 --> 00:10:33.455
Check yourself.

00:10:33.975 --> 00:10:35.428
Why does a grid start with

00:10:35.428 --> 00:10:36.880
some coin as well as cash?

00:10:37.044 --> 00:10:38.329
Because the sell orders

00:10:38.329 --> 00:10:39.837
need coin you already hold.

00:10:40.855 --> 00:10:42.363
In the example pair, why is

00:10:42.363 --> 00:10:44.039
the net about eight and a half

00:10:44.039 --> 00:10:45.715
dollars and not the whole gap?

00:10:46.146 --> 00:10:47.710
The two fees come out first.

00:10:48.872 --> 00:10:50.983
If a daily close is outside the band,

00:10:50.983 --> 00:10:53.167
through the top or the bottom, and the

00:10:53.167 --> 00:10:55.350
next close is still outside, you stop

00:10:55.350 --> 00:10:57.461
the bot and follow the written rule.

00:10:58.699 --> 00:10:59.449
Your turn.

00:10:59.895 --> 00:11:01.627
On paper, write the top and the

00:11:01.627 --> 00:11:03.582
bottom, one gap, and the stop rule.

00:11:04.686 --> 00:11:06.417
Say what you will do if a daily

00:11:06.417 --> 00:11:08.037
close leaves the band and the

00:11:08.037 --> 00:11:09.602
next close is still outside.

00:11:09.933 --> 00:11:11.162
You stop the bot, then

00:11:11.162 --> 00:11:12.335
you follow that rule.

00:11:13.345 --> 00:11:15.412
No real order is sent in this lesson.

00:11:15.899 --> 00:11:17.802
Paper practice comes in Lesson

00:11:17.802 --> 00:11:19.413
7, and real money only after

00:11:19.413 --> 00:11:21.242
your written graduation rule.

00:11:22.442 --> 00:11:24.342
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:11:24.673 --> 00:11:25.682
You draw the idea.

00:11:26.202 --> 00:11:27.996
If a screen appears later, it

00:11:27.996 --> 00:11:29.711
should be a copy of the page,

00:11:29.711 --> 00:11:31.271
and only on paper or demo.

00:11:32.471 --> 00:11:34.304
A grid bot places waiting buys

00:11:34.304 --> 00:11:36.357
below the price and waiting sells

00:11:36.357 --> 00:11:38.337
above it, inside a band you choose.

00:11:39.537 --> 00:11:40.654
A finished pair buys

00:11:40.654 --> 00:11:41.939
lower and sells higher.

00:11:42.146 --> 00:11:43.766
The fees come out of the gap.

00:11:44.055 --> 00:11:46.234
In the example that was about eight and

00:11:46.234 --> 00:11:48.469
a half dollars, and it is not a promise.

00:11:49.321 --> 00:11:50.717
Leave through the top and

00:11:50.717 --> 00:11:51.891
you hold mostly cash.

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:53.681
Leave through the bottom

00:11:53.681 --> 00:11:55.077
and you hold mostly coin.

00:11:56.118 --> 00:11:58.356
If a daily close leaves the band and the

00:11:58.356 --> 00:12:00.454
next close is still outside, you stop

00:12:00.454 --> 00:12:02.577
the bot and follow the rule you wrote.

00:12:03.751 --> 00:12:06.112
Bring a notebook, and no secrets: no

00:12:06.112 --> 00:12:08.726
seed phrase, private key or API secret.

00:12:09.246 --> 00:12:11.103
Those are the words or keys that

00:12:11.103 --> 00:12:12.817
unlock a wallet or an account.

00:12:13.867 --> 00:12:15.560
The pair, in the next lesson,

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.175
is the two things you swap,

00:12:17.175 --> 00:12:18.944
like bitcoin and US dollars.

00:12:19.994 --> 00:12:22.229
Next lesson: What you are going to need.

00:12:22.617 --> 00:12:24.182
Bring your notes: your band,

00:12:24.182 --> 00:12:25.802
your gaps and your stop rule.

00:12:26.075 --> 00:12:27.432
Keep the word Example on

00:12:27.432 --> 00:12:28.722
every practice figure.

00:12:29.242 --> 00:12:31.197
Next lesson you will write the page

00:12:31.197 --> 00:12:33.209
of what you need, before any screen.

